# ============================================================================
# Browser4 LLM configuration — template
# ============================================================================
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE: while it sits in "conf-available/" it has no effect.
# Only its copy in the sibling directory is read, and that copy is read once,
# when the backend starts:
#
#     <app data dir>/config/conf-enabled/application-private.properties
#     e.g. ~/.browser4/config/conf-enabled/application-private.properties
#
# `browser4-cli doctor --fix` creates and enables that copy for you, and
# `browser4-cli doctor` prints the exact path in use plus the key that won.
#
# How to use this file:
#   1. Uncomment exactly ONE provider block below and fill in a real API key.
#   2. Restart the backend: `browser4-cli stop` (then any command restarts it).
#   3. Verify the routing: `browser4-cli doctor` →
#      "Configured keys" / "Selected key" / "Active model".
#
# Configure EXACTLY ONE provider. When several provider keys are present, the
# first one in the built-in detection order wins — `openai` comes after the
# dedicated providers such as `deepseek`, so a leftover DeepSeek key silently
# wins over OPENAI_*. Decide explicitly with:
#     llm.provider=openai              # select one (browser4-base 4.11.20+)
#     llm.provider.deny.list=deepseek  # skip one (any version)
#
# Environment variables work as well, and are the recommended home for secrets:
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY, DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, VOLCENGINE_API_KEY, ...
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## OpenRouter (default) — 300+ models behind a single key
# openrouter.api.key=sk-or-v1-...
# openrouter.model.name=bytedance-seed/seed-1.6
# openrouter.base.url=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

## DeepSeek
# deepseek.api.key=sk-...
# deepseek.model.name=deepseek-v4-flash
# deepseek.base.url=https://api.deepseek.com/v1

## OpenAI-compatible — any OpenAI-compatible endpoint: DeepInfra, Groq, vLLM,
## LM Studio, a corporate gateway, ...
# openai.api.key=sk-...
# openai.model.name=gpt-5.6-sol
# openai.base.url=https://api.openai.com/v1
#
# Example — DeepInfra:
# openai.api.key=<your deepinfra key>
# openai.model.name=deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash
# openai.base.url=https://api.deepinfra.com/v1/openai

## Aliyun DashScope (Qwen) — also an OpenAI-compatible endpoint
# openai.api.key=sk-...
# openai.model.name=qwen-plus
# openai.base.url=https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1

## Volcengine (ByteDance / Doubao)
# volcengine.api.key=...
# volcengine.model.name=doubao-seed-2-0-pro-260215
# volcengine.base.url=https://ark.cn-beijing.volces.com/api/v3

## Full provider list, precedence and troubleshooting: docs/config.md
